ref 17592186045417] [17592186521199 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c351ba7c-4c6f-5399-9980-cd006f2d48fe" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521211 #edb/ref 1080 "0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521211 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521211 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c81bffa8-6d28-5db1-a4e4-943e85fac37c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521387 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520808 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521387 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520958 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521387 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520996 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521387 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521168 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521387 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521387 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521387 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521387 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186521211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521387 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "81425c09-b875-5245-8a44-a234fc04ecfd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521421 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520786 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521421 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521421 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520953 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521421 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520963 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521421 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521421 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521421 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521421 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186521022 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521421 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "bce8cadb-6f17-5458-a146-66e868571308" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520930 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521065 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521109 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521144 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521451 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186521149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521451 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521451 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521451 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186521149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521451 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fd517342-4196-5078-a01c-54f228cf9d0a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521464 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521387 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521464 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162232" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521464 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521464 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the circulation $Γ$ of the vector field $F(x,y,z)=x\\,i-z\\,k$ along the closed curve $C$ given by $r(t)=({t}^{2}-t)\\,i+({t}^{3}-{t}^{2})\\,j+k$ for $t\\in [0,1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521464 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "19360ab0-63c4-5cd8-9a4a-b29910944cd3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521464 #edb/ref 1074 "The circulation $Γ$ measures the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along a *closed* curve $C.$\nIt is given by the formula\n\n$$\nΓ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r={\\int }_{a}^{b}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx={t}^{2}-t,\\,y={t}^{3}-{t}^{2},\\,z=1.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =x\\,i-z\\,k \\\\  & =({t}^{2}-t)\\,i-1\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{2}-t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{3}-{t}^{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1)\\,k \\\\  & =(2t-1)\\,i+(3{t}^{2}-2t)\\,j+0\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(({t}^{2}-t)\\,i-\\,k)\\cdot ((2t-1)\\,i+(3{t}^{2}-2t)\\,j) \\\\  & =({t}^{2}-t)\\cdot (2t-1)+0\\cdot (3{t}^{2}-2t)+(-1)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =({t}^{2}-t)(2t-1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Γ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({t}^{2}-t)(2t-1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\frac{({t}^{2}-t)^{2}}{2}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(0-0) \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521469 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521469 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162363" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521469 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521469 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $C$ be the intersection of the hyperbolic paraboloid $z={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ and the boundary of the infinite vertical column enclosed by the planes $x=\\pm 1,$ $y=\\pm 2.$ Given that the curve $C$ is oriented counter-clockwise when viewed from above and $\\text{curl}\\,F=⟨y,\\,x,\\,2⟩,$ the circulation of $F$ along $C$ can be written as \n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr=\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521469 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "22c4166d-7812-5cc0-89d7-bc30157982f0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521469 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $S$ be an oriented piecewise-smooth surface bounded by a simple, closed, piecewise-smooth boundary $C$ with positive orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $S,$ then Stokes' theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∬}_{S}\\text{curl}\\,F\\cdot \\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nThere are many surfaces whose boundary is the curve $C$ representing the intersection of the paraboloid $z={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}$ and the boundary of our infinite vertical column. One such surface is our paraboloid $S$ with the equation \n\n$$\nz=g(x,y)={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the partial derivatives of the graph $z=g(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂g}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})=2x \\\\ \\frac{∂g}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-{y}^{2})=-2y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the equation $z=g(x,y)$ into expression for $\\text{curl}\\,F:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{curl}\\,F\\,{|}_{z=g(x,y)} & =⟨y,\\,x,\\,2⟩{|}_{z={x}^{2}-{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =⟨y,\\,x,\\,2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{{y}_{⏟}}_{P},\\,{{x}_{⏟}}_{Q},\\,{{2}_{⏟}}_{R}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\text{curl}\\,F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}(-P\\frac{∂g}{∂x}-Q\\frac{∂g}{∂y}+R)\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}(-y\\cdot (2x)-x\\cdot (-2y)+2)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}2\\,\\text{d}A,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is region enclosed by the projection of $C$ onto the $xy$-plane, shown below.\n\n![](images/5f/5f2f4cb03b3b0232c9debd1f4ed64bd683fe788ccba16cfbe395d9c3b629972d.png)\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}2\\,\\text{d}A & ={\\int }_{-1}^{1}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}\\,2\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521475 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186521451 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521475 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162890" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521475 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521475 #edb/ref 1071 "Let $S$ be an oriented piecewise-smooth surface bounded by the closed curve $C$ with positive orientation and parametrization $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,k$ for $t\\in [0,2\\pi ).$\nGiven that $F(x,y,z)=2z\\,i+x\\,j+3y\\,k,$ evaluate the integral\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}\\text{curl}\\,F\\cdot \\text{d}S.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521475 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2bdcc65b-8401-5044-8aa5-c9a7e37ffa6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521475 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $S$ be an oriented piecewise-smooth surface bounded by a simple, closed, piecewise-smooth boundary $C$ with positive orientation. If a vector field $F$ has continuous partial derivatives for all its components in an open region in space that contains $S,$ then Stokes' theorem states that\n\n$$\n{∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr={∬}_{S}\\text{curl}\\,F\\cdot \\text{d}S.\n$$\n\nAlong the curve $C,$ we have\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,z=2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t.\n$$\n\nSo,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t)) & =2z\\,i+x\\,j+3y\\,k \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nComputing ${r}^{′}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,k \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t) & =(4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k)\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,k) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\cdot 2\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+6\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\cdot (-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t) \\\\  & =-4\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+2{cos}^{2}⁡t-12{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)+2{cos}^{2}⁡t+2{sin}^{2}⁡t-14{sin}^{2}⁡t \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-14{sin}^{2}⁡t+2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}\\text{curl}\\,F\\cdot \\text{d}S & ={∮}_{C}F\\cdot dr \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }F(r(t))\\cdot {r}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-14{sin}^{2}⁡t+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-7(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)+2)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }(-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t-5+7\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={[\\operatorname{cos}⁡2t-5t+\\frac{7}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡2t]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =(1-5(2\\pi )+0)-(1-5(0)+0) \\\\  & =-10\\pi \\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521580 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186521614 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521580 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "18ae8c42-183b-544f-aacc-4eaa3f1d420a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521580 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186521464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521583 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "241fd184-8019-52bd-8c7e-c4c658c038e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521583 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186521475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521614 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186521642 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521614 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7448047a-c9c1-58cc-8181-6b27db0e6a80" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521614 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186521469 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521621 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186521580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521621 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "840ab71a-6f7d-5c82-b51d-fda507e2a915" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521621 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134130 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521642 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186521583 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521642 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cb01237b-4d73-5b10-94f4-c0c4f3fdada5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186521642 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134134 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
